#N canvas 0 0 720 520 10;
#X text 12 8 mpein - MIDI Polyphonic Expression (MPE v1.0) parser;
#X text 12 28 Universal and object-agnostic: eats a raw MIDI message stream (the app's [midi-raw] bridge receiver delivers every complete channel message) and emits per-note voice events on ONE selector-ized outlet - any patch decides what the voices do. Split with [route note pitch slide press midi zone]. Channels 1..16 \, no zone gating (devices that never declare a zone still work). CC74 = slide \, CC2 = pressure \, aftertouch maps to press too \, bend = continuous semitones (+/- bendrange \, default 48). A note down carries slide/press snapshots right after it. RPN 0\,6 / 0\,7 zone declarations are tracked and echoed on the zone selector;
#X text 20 220 hand-fed test bytes below (a real device arrives from [midi-raw]) - statuses: 145 = note on ch2 \, 226 = bend ch3 \, 178 = CC ch3 \, 210 = aftertouch ch3;
#X obj 20 260 mpein;
#X msg 20 300 status;
#X msg 80 300 clear;
#X msg 140 300 bendrange 24;
#X msg 250 300 145 60 100;
#X msg 340 300 146 60 0;
#X msg 430 300 226 0 96;
#X msg 20 330 178 74 90;
#X msg 110 330 210 80;
#X msg 190 330 178 64 64;
#X obj 20 380 route note pitch slide press midi zone;
#X obj 20 430 print note;
#X obj 120 430 print pitch;
#X obj 220 430 print slide;
#X obj 320 430 print press;
#X obj 430 430 print midi;
#X obj 520 430 print zone;
#X text 20 470 What the voices do is yours to wire: drive synth/voice objects \, sequencers \, anything. Non-dimension CC bytes (sustain \, mod wheel \, volume) ride the midi passthrough as ch*128+value;
#X connect 4 0 3 0;
#X connect 5 0 3 0;
#X connect 6 0 3 0;
#X connect 7 0 3 0;
#X connect 8 0 3 0;
#X connect 9 0 3 0;
#X connect 10 0 3 0;
#X connect 11 0 3 0;
#X connect 12 0 3 0;
#X connect 3 0 13 0;
#X connect 13 0 14 0;
#X connect 13 1 15 0;
#X connect 13 2 16 0;
#X connect 13 3 17 0;
#X connect 13 4 18 0;
#X connect 13 5 19 0;
